50,3,1,talk,Servas,,"The candidates are A: Clinic Scheduler, B: Harvest Sensor, C: Fabric Loop, and D: Ledger Bridge. I find D most appealing for reporting.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Asuka,,D aligns with our successful exit profile in financial tooling. A and B also show better retention in my data.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Minako,,"C is a nightmare for our reserves; it requires depots and hourly crews, which led to our only write-off.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Mio,,"B and C both need field or facility crews, which my research shows are nearly impossible to recruit quickly.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Toshio,,A will be trapped in security reviews for months. B and D are much faster to deploy.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Toshio, if A is delayed, then D becomes the strongest software option.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, if B is out due to staffing, and C is out due to operations, we are left with A and D.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, A is a subscription model, which we know is poor security for our credit line. D is more aligned with financial reconciliation.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Mio,,I definitely vote against B and C. D sounds like it doesn't need a field crew!,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Minako, D is also a financial tool, but it doesn't necessarily hold the same medical-grade records that A does.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Servas,,D avoids the audit fees of hardware and the security delays of medical data. It is the most efficient choice.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I agree. D fits the exit profile and avoids the retention issues of the shopkeeper tools.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Minako,,D is the most fiscally responsible choice given our current reserve pressure.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Mio,,I'm voting for D! No more searching for seasonal crews for me.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Toshio,,D is the only one that avoids both the security bottleneck and the hardware delivery risk.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Servas,,I vote for D.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I vote for D.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Minako,,I vote for D.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Mio,,I vote for D.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I vote for D.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
